{"title":"2017 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(combinational)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (combinational)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(regular_probability)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (regular probability)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Complementary_Counting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Complementary Counting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(List_&amp;_Count)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (List &amp; Count)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also:\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also:</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A box contains five cards, numbered 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5. Three cards are selected randomly without replacement from the box. What is the probability that 4 is the largest value selected? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d49dc816b9fd6ccfb6438034a0a9d8fe291a9446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{1}{10}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{3}{10}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{2}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"390\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28combinational.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(combinational)\">Solution 1 (combinational)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (combinational)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5fefbb8ab341ebf885d0070f5c69a6e8c292b63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> possible groups of cards that can be selected. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the largest card selected, then the other two cards must be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, for a total <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/50257e1113399bb38a23519393448f182d5f410d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> groups of cards. Then, the probability is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2dbee4597e2282e1485c20c894122fd3da96139.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{{\\dbinom{3}{2}}}{{\\dbinom{5}{3}}}} = \\boxed{{\\textbf{(C) }} {\\frac{3}{10}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -51px\" width=\"134\" height=\"111\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28regular_probability.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(regular_probability)\">Solution 2 (regular probability)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (regular probability)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>P (no 5)= <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fd03d5b164ae8b40db27a6f8ddb20d9d43f95fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> * <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> * <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. This is the fraction of total cases with no fives.\np (no 4 and no 5)= <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac40ce1434cda0943c408cc185f5976212d95801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> * <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dbaa7bcbcc129e8efc76dbce04421b1047eb3577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> * <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b738b598473388e5da7bdf29b3a27910f8307c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c00e9e2066800d5a55332a7fb456073bbce0a08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. This is the intersection of no fours and no fives. Subtract the fraction of no fours and no fives from that of no fives. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4b8966b62aed61b37bcded62735f96e6f2a3d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5} - \\frac{1}{10} = \\frac{3}{10} = \\boxed{{\\textbf{(C) }} {\\frac{3}{10}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"198\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Simple)\">Solution 3 (Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Pick any desirable situation. Let's say you first draw a 4, then a 3, then a 2. The probability of that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d129a7b3c0bf9fbd0693afdd426a66d2a0a8c3ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> * <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> * <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f60bedc5b5b46bbd2652971d30b4e69bfad748a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. And for this case, it doesn't matter if you first draw a 3 or a 2. The probability of drawing a 4, a 3, and a 2 in any order is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f60bedc5b5b46bbd2652971d30b4e69bfad748a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>Next, list other desirable situations. You can draw a 4, 3, 1, or a 4,2,1, regardless of order. So, our desirable situations are 4,3,2, then 4,3,1, and lastly 4,2,1, regardless of order.\n</p><p>Now, for each desirable situation, there are 3!=6 ways to arrange the numbers. That means that there are 6 ways to arrange 4,3,1, then 6 ways to arrange 4,2,1, and 6 ways to arrange 4,3,2. 6*3=18, which means, accounting for order, there are 18 desirable outcomes. \n</p><p>The probability of each desirable outcome is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f60bedc5b5b46bbd2652971d30b4e69bfad748a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. Since there are 18 of them, the probability that 4 is the highest value selected is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f60bedc5b5b46bbd2652971d30b4e69bfad748a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />*18, which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3eca92e03419c6e67bce685f48c906f7bd5fb324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{18}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, which simplifies to the answer,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f0cf2a41ca6fbaafe3d21b823a9bed30c7272fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>This might be a lengthy explanation, but the idea behind it is pretty simple, and it doesn't take long for it to find the answer. Wish you luck on the AMC8! ~Evžen D.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Complementary_Counting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Complementary_Counting)\">Solution 4 (Complementary Counting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Complementary Counting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First we have to find the probability that we choose a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. One of the three numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the other two have to be chosen from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed123aec81a19e7c53d2af259f3b30d52b9b6d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> so the number of sets with 5 as the largest number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c9b68a04fadb4cbe90954c537de424c1519ef51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{4}{2}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" />. The number of ways to choose a set of three from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/2/d2289231163b75dca0daf0f842ee0fba6f289fc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5894fb25890d6b71779b81a580a39fe1b1cdcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{5}{3}=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" />, so that means that the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the highest number in the set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b319a513d6bcf45a66d76b403e77465bcb00bd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10/10-6/10=4/10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /> right... nope! This is wrong because one of these sets that doesn't have 5 as the largest value also doesn't have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as it's largest value! We have over counted! So, we find the number of ways where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> isn't in the set either. There is only one possibility because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/1424e6f044406ae5403c6e9f419e013b4e3c43a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{3}{3}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" />. This means that there are only three ways to have a set with 4 as the largest value, so we find the probability to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/272956fa930620411cc4f7d8adac00c138d69c8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{{\\textbf{(C) }} {\\frac{3}{10}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Shriyans.Chowdhury\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28List_.26_Count.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(List_&amp;_Count)\">Solution 5 (List &amp; Count)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (List &amp; Count)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Step 1: List every possible group of 3 cards.\n</p><p>Since there are only 5 cards, list every possible set of 3 numbers:<br />\n</p><p>1, 2, 3<br />\n1, 2, 4<br />\n1, 2, 5<br />\n1, 3, 4<br />\n1, 3, 5<br />\n1, 4, 5<br />\n2, 3, 4<br />\n2, 3, 5<br />\n2, 4, 5<br />\n3, 4, 5<br />\n</p><p>Step 2: Find the groups where 4 is the biggest number.\n</p><p>1, 2, 4 ✓<br />\n1, 3, 4 ✓<br />\n2, 3, 4 ✓<br />\n</p><p>Step 3: Turn it into a probability.\n</p><p>Probability just means: (number of groups that work) out of (total number of groups).\nSo the probability is 3 out of 10, or 3/10.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/P-K9AEAuhNY\">https://youtu.be/P-K9AEAuhNY</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/OOdK-nOzaII?t=1237\">https://youtu.be/OOdK-nOzaII?t=1237</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/M9kj4ztWbwo\">https://youtu.be/M9kj4ztWbwo</a></li></ul>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FN9qkU62a9U\">https://youtu.be/FN9qkU62a9U</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F935tcVcXvY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F935tcVcXvY</a>   ~davidxxxx</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also:\">See Also:</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also:\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8\" title=\"2017 AMC 8\">2017 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title